{"content":[{"c":["REHOB (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Northernmost territory explored by the Israelite spies prior to occupation of Canaan (",{"href":"?bref=Num.13.21","r":"Num.13.21","rawR":"Num.13.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.13.21","value":"Num.13.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 13:21"},"). It agrees with the location of Beth-rehob (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.18.28","r":"Judg.18.28","rawR":"Judg.18.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.18.28","value":"Judg.18.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 18:28"},") and is mentioned with Zobah and Maacah as an opponent of David in the Ammonite war (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.10.6-8","r":"2Sam.10.6-8","rawR":"2Sam.10.6-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.10.6-8","value":"2Sam.10.6-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 10:6-8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Two cities belonging to Asher’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.28-30","r":"Josh.19.28-30","rawR":"Josh.19.28-30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.28-30","value":"Josh.19.28-30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:28-30"},"). One was given to the Levitical family of Gershon (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.31","r":"Josh.21.31","rawR":"Josh.21.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.31","value":"Josh.21.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:31"},") and became a city of refuge (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.75","r":"1Chr.6.75","rawR":"1Chr.6.75","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.75","value":"1Chr.6.75"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:75"},"). The other remained in Canaanite hands (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.31","r":"Judg.1.31","rawR":"Judg.1.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.31","value":"Judg.1.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 1:31"},"). Some scholars identify the references as one city."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," Cities of Refuge; Levitical Cities."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"RehobPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 13:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.13.21","rawQueryValue":"Num.13.21","sourceRefExact":"Num.13.21"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 18:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.18.28","rawQueryValue":"Judg.18.28","sourceRefExact":"Judg.18.28"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 10:6-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.10.6-8","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.10.6-8","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.10.6-8"},{"anchorText":"Jos 19:28-30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.28-30","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.28-30","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.28-30"},{"anchorText":"Jos 21:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.31","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.31","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.31"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:75","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.75","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.75","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.75"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 1:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.31","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.31","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c32e53adca7d64e6801931480aa65095bed395647afe15de65515e2e72bd45bd","sourceItemName":"RehobPlace","sourceItemOrder":94,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"RehobPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Rehob (Place)","title":"Rehob (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}